ologo/40657026/40657026-1768486187830-f8f544fbc7c46.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:18:59</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The MAD Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>AI Takeover Isn&#x27;t a 2029 Problem, It&#x27;s a 2028 Problem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ryan Greenblatt predicts AI R&amp;D will be fully automated between 2028 and 2031, with progress doubling every 4-5 times per year, making takeover risk extremely high; he proposes a US-China compute transparency agreement as a slowdown plan.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI risk</span><span class=\"tag\">superintelligence prediction</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"After GLP-1: Injections Are No Longer a Barrier, Peptide Drugs Enter a New Era Injectable drugs are no longer a barrier; peptide drugs are expanding from weight loss to exercise mimetics, neural regulation, and beyond. Scientists caution: beyond GLP, data are still sparse, and approval cycles could take up to 20 years. From Our Neurons to Yours From Our Neurons to Yours After Ozempic: the revolution in peptide science | Jonathan Long peptide drugs GLP-1 exercise mimetics weight loss drug discovery biotech GLP-1 / glucagon-like peptide-1 Lac-Phe / lactate phenylalanine Unimolecular polyagonist AGRP neurons / agouti-related peptide neurons POMC neurons / proopiomelanocortin neurons MOTRPAC / Molecular Transducers of Physical Activity Consortium\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-fromourneurons-glp-1之后-肽科学正在开启医学新大门/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://storage.buzzsprout.com/vqsbkvixwt8cyaq4nqd5od1ubzc3?.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">49:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<d